  "movementSpeed": 139,
  "movementSpeedNote": "OWNER 2026-08-14: 260 was \"way too fast\". The premise behind it was wrong: the claim that all three Act 1 surfaces share cameraWorldWidth=208 holds for the TOWN, which sets VIEW_W=208 and zooms to fit, but NOT for the overworld/dungeon, where the shipped camera runs at zoom 1 so worldView equals the canvas CSS size -- about 390 world px on the owner's 390pt iPhone. At the same 260 px/s that is 1.25 screen-widths per second in town against 0.67 in the dungeon: 1.9x faster ON SCREEN, which is what he felt. Matched by screen-widths per second instead of raw px/s: 260 * 208/390 = 139. Note this calibration is tied to a ~390pt-wide screen, because the town's view is a fixed world width while the overworld's scales with the device.",
